-- BASELINE MIGRATION — the only hand-edited file in this folder.
--
-- Generated by drizzle-kit from src/db/schema.ts, then adjusted from
-- `CREATE TABLE` to `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`. That edit is what lets an
-- existing database adopt migrations without being rebuilt.
--
-- Why it is required: before this, the schema was created by an idempotent
-- initDatabase() DDL block at startup, so live databases already have all nine
-- tables and no __drizzle_migrations row. drizzle's migrator applies every
-- migration whose timestamp is newer than the last recorded one, inside ONE
-- transaction, and rolls the whole thing back on error — so a plain
-- `CREATE TABLE` here would raise "table kb_brands already exists" and abort
-- startup on every database that predates this commit. With IF NOT EXISTS the
-- baseline is a no-op against those, is recorded as applied, and the schema and
-- the migration history are back in agreement.
--
-- Do NOT copy this pattern into later migrations. Every subsequent file must be
-- the verbatim output of `npm run db:generate`: from here on a schema change is
-- a reviewed diff, not a guess about what the target database already contains.

